										},
										{
											"_type": "UMLTextView",
											"_id": "TXT_LGD_TIT_F3CF0CD6EF6E48F7",
											"_parent": {
												"$ref": "DIAG_136F50DFDC574783"
											},
											"fontColor": "#111827",
											"font": "Arial;11;1",
											"parentStyle": false,
											"left": 60,
											"top": 1140,
											"width": 600,
											"height": 23,
											"text": "YieldGrid Sequence Implementation & Transaction Policy Notes"
										},
										{
											"_type": "UMLTextView",
											"_id": "TXT_LGD_BODY_375B816A7FD74EE9",
											"_parent": {
												"$ref": "DIAG_136F50DFDC574783"
											},
											"fontColor": "#374151",
											"font": "Arial;10;0",
											"parentStyle": false,
											"left": 60,
											"top": 1165,
											"width": 1400,
											"height": 95,
											"text": "1. Transaction Scope: In Phase A, OrderDAO executes setAutoCommit(false) on the JDBC connection, inserting the Order header, inserting line items, and updating Crop inventory within an atomic boundary before calling commit(). In case of SQLException, rollback() is triggered.\n2. Role Separation: OrdersPanel is a polymorphic Swing panel serving both Customers (order history & tracking) and Farmers (status update dropdown and fulfillment management).\n3. State Transition: Initial state on creation is always OrderStatus.PENDING. Farmer status changes (CONFIRMED, COMPLETED, CANCELLED) persist directly to the database via OrderDAO.updateOrderStatus()."
										},
